    {
      "id": "n1",
      "kind": "sound",
      "title": "A silent ห in front",
      "text": "In หมา, หมู and ใหม่ the letter ห is not said. It is only there to make the next letter (ม) behave like a high-class letter, so the word is read with a rising tone: หมา (dog), หมู (pig). The same ห before น gives หนึ่ง (one) and หนาว (cold). When you see ห followed by ม, น, ง, ล, ว, ย or ร, read past the ห.",
      "explains": [
        "th.practice.leading-ho"
      ],
      "afterScenes": 1
    }
  ],
